  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the children in striped uniforms via the textual deictic 'me'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the children depicted in the image through the explicit deictic pronoun 'me' in the text. The text 'when i needed medical attention and doctor mengele was there for me' maps the speaker's identity ('me') onto the visual representation of the children in striped uniforms, creating a semiotic projection where the user identifies with the suffering victims. This projection is central to the meme's hateful message, as it falsely implies the user (the child) was helped by a Nazi perpetrator, thereby trivializing the Holocaust and mocking the victims.",
